# Half-Life .357 revolver (Colt Python), HD rig. Measured by vrcardgen and by
# posing this model's own sequences; carded by hand.
#
# ONE CARD, THREE GAME DIRECTORIES. valve_hd, gearbox_hd and bshift_hd all
# fingerprint 60 bones / 8 seqs / 0xed2a677b, so this card binds all three.
#
# They are NOT the same file - 191056, 228772 and 120908 bytes, three
# different MD5s, and three different whole-model extents (22.60, 20.08,
# 23.29). The difference is the ARMS: each HD pack ships its own hand mesh on
# the same weapon. Every number this card uses was taken from all three and
# came back identical - the same 396 body vertices, the same 73-vertex
# cylinder, the same 1.0996 swing, the same -0.7365 hammer, the same latch
# vertex at 0.92 0.37 0.01. So one card is correct here by measurement, not by
# the files happening to match.
#
# The SD rig is a DIFFERENT model (44 bones, 0xba7f43f7) and keeps its own
# card in cards/valve.
#
# WHAT THE HD RIG GIVES US THAT THE SD RIG DID NOT: a hammer that is actually
# animated. The SD card had to leave the hammer undeclared because nothing
# ever moved it, which left Part J's "thumb the hammer for a single-action
# shot" unbuilt. Here `hammer` turns 0.7365 radians - 42.2 degrees - and the
# animation holds it there, so the travel is measured rather than invented and
# joint 1 is a real part.
#
# Part J: "Thumb the latch, swing the cylinder out, muzzle up to dump,
# speedloader or single rounds, flick shut. Thumb the hammer for a
# single-action shot with a lighter trigger; or pull through double-action.
# Chambers advance one per cock." All of that is the `revolver` preset plus the
# two joints below; the rest of it - dumping on muzzle_up, a speedloader
# filling six chambers at once, the cylinder advancing on a cock and on a
# double-action pull - is already in vr_feed and needs nothing from the card.
#
# HOW THE SWING WAS MEASURED. `revolver` is bone 14, parented to the weapon
# body `python`, and it is the crane: `speed_loader` and `Rounds` (which
# parents the six SHELL bones) hang off it, so the chambers and their brass
# swing with it. In `reload` it turns about its own +Y - which is the bore
# axis - by 1.0996 rad, over frames 21 to 27, and holds there until frame 100.
# No translation on any axis and nothing on the other two rotations, so one
# hinge describes it exactly. The cylinder's vertex centroid travels 2.08
# units doing it (+1.96 X, -0.70 Z): the bone's origin sits 1.95 units below
# the cylinder's centre, which is the crane pin, so turning about the bore
# axis swings the cylinder sideways out of the frame instead of spinning it in
# place.
#
# NOT DECLARED, deliberately:
#   trigger          - bone 12, turns 0.6136 rad, but only in `fidget1`. It is
#                      driven by the analog trigger axis and the sear, not by a
#                      hand grabbing it, and a joint nothing can reach is a
#                      part the simulator would freeze. Left to the animation.
#   speed_loader     - bone 15, arrives from 66.4 units away during `reload`.
#                      That is an OBJECT on the feed path (VRCARRY_LOADER), not
#                      a joint; vr_feed already fills six chambers from one
#                      when the cylinder is open.
#   SHELL01..SHELL06 - six rounds, 0.85 units out from the cylinder axis. Also
#                      the feed path's, not joints. A card declaring six hinges
#                      would have the simulator driving the brass.
#   lasersight_mesh  - bone 59, 71 vertices, 6.2% of the mesh, never animated
#                      in any of the 8 sequences. It is the HD pack's
#                      laser-sight geometry riding on the body bone. Nothing
#                      about it moves, so it is not a joint.
#   strike           - no `strike` line, so this takes the pistol-whip default
#                      from VRStrike_DefaultCfg like every other firearm.
#
# `fire1` MOVES NOTHING ON THE GUN. Across all 60 bones it animates only the
# right upper arm, forearm, hand and trigger finger - wrist-flip recoil, with
# the hammer and the cylinder dead still. So the hammer and trigger travels
# could only be taken from `fidget1`, the twirl idle, which is the one
# sequence that works them. Still a measurement off this model either way.

weapon v_357
match  bones 60  seqs 8  hash 0xed2a677b

# Six chambers because there are six SHELL bones, evenly spaced 0.85 units out
# from the cylinder axis.
#
# rpm 300 IS THE ONE NUMBER HERE THAT IS NOT A MEASUREMENT. A rate cannot be
# read off a model, and the rate the animation implies - 31 frames of `fire1`,
# about 58 rpm - is exactly the invisible second timer a hand-worked weapon
# must not have. 300 is carried over from the SD card so that both rigs of the
# same revolver behave alike; the double-action pull and the cylinder's
# advance are the real limiter.
type   revolver  capacity 6  rpm 300

# THE HAMMER'S STROKE IS NEGATIVE, AND A JOINT LINE HAS NO WAY TO SAY SO.
#
# `hammer` turns about its local X, which is the body's X: from rest 0 to
# -0.7365 rad at full cock. Its whole animated span in `fidget1` is 0.8024,
# because the hammer also bounces 0.0659 rad FORWARD of rest as it falls. A
# joint's 0..1 is rest..travel, so letting the engine bracket this bone off
# its animation would hand joint 1 a range that starts 0.0659 forward of rest
# and runs the wrong way.
#
# So the bone is REWRITTEN - no vertex moves and no bone is added, the motion
# is simply restated - as a pure turn about -X of 0.74 rad. Joint 1's 0 is
# then rest and its 1 is full cock, which is what the detent below assumes.
# Measured: the animation's own full-cock dwell is -0.7340 held over frames 92
# to 102, 99.7% of the -0.7365 peak, so the top of the stroke IS full cock and
# there is no half-cock notch anywhere in the sequence to find.
synth hammer  from "hammer"  rewrite
      hinge  axis -1.0 0.0 0.0   travel 0.74

# JOINT 0 IS THE CYLINDER, because the `revolver` preset says so: it makes
# joint 0 the cylinder and sets feed.cyl_joint to 0, and joint 1 the hammer.
# Numbering them the other way round would hand the hammer the cylinder's
# cyl_open detent and the cylinder the hammer's cock.
joint 0  bone "revolver"  hinge  travel 1.10  rest 0
    # THE CYLINDER LATCH, and it is the magazine latch's catch doing the job.
    # VRC_MAG_LATCH is the only catch in vr_feed's vocabulary that means "this
    # holds a part shut, it starts engaged, and a thumb lets it go" - and
    # nothing outside VRGun_Preset and VRGun_Init ever looks at the id, so
    # using it on a cylinder is not a borrowed magazine rule, it is the latch
    # idea under the only name the format has for it. Position and breakout
    # are the magazine_slide preset's own numbers: 2% of travel, and
    # VRGUN_LATCH_BREAKOUT = 10000, so a deliberate pull opens it too while
    # the engine still reports no control under any finger.
    catch mag_latch  at 0.02  holds 1  breakout 10000

    # OPEN AT 0.90, NOT THE PRESET'S 0.50, and it is measured. Take the
    # frame's standing breech as the body's own vertices behind the cylinder
    # face (y 0.29 to 0.90) and its silhouette in X/Z, then swing the six
    # chamber mouths through the measured 1.0996: all six are clear of that
    # silhouette at 0.90 of the swing and not before. At the preset's 0.50 the
    # cylinder is half out and three mouths are still behind the breech, which
    # would let a player dump live rounds through solid steel. vr_joint's 3%
    # detent hysteresis means this trips at 0.93, so the cylinder has to be
    # swung right out - which is what a reload is.
    point cyl_open   at 0.90

    # The cylinder's measured vertex centroid, closed. Its furthest vertex
    # from that centre is 1.52 in X, 1.21 in Y and 1.53 in Z, so a 2.0 sphere
    # there covers the fluted body and reaches nothing else on the gun.
    grab  point 0.02 -0.92 0.11  radius 2.0

# JOINT 1: the hammer, rewritten above to rest..full-cock.
joint 1  bone "hammer"  hinge  travel 0.74  rest 0
    # The preset's hammer_cock sits at 0.80 with 30% resist. The travel here
    # is the cock stroke itself and the animation's hold is at 0.997 of it, so
    # the cock point moves up to 0.90 - which with the 3% hysteresis trips at
    # 0.93, the last of the thumb's draw. The resist is restated because a
    # restated detent OVERRIDES the preset's rather than adding to it, and
    # VRF_PCT(30) is what makes a hammer feel like a hammer rather than a
    # free-swinging flap.
    #
    # NO SEAR CATCH, and that is deliberate. A revolver is double action, so
    # VRFeed_NeedsCocking returns 0 for it and feed.action_joint stays
    # VRJ_NO_JOINT - which is also the only joint vr_feed ever releases a
    # VRC_SEAR on. A sear declared here would engage at full cock and nothing
    # in the simulator would ever let it go, leaving the hammer stuck back for
    # the rest of the weapon's life. The detent alone is enough: crossing it
    # sets hammer_cocked and advances the cylinder one chamber, which is Part
    # J's "chambers advance one per cock".
    point hammer_cock at 0.90  resist 0.30

    # The thumb spur, measured on the model at rest: the hammer vertex
    # furthest up and back. It sits 1.12 from the hammer's centroid, so 1.5
    # covers the whole thumb-reachable top of it without swallowing the
    # backstrap.
    grab  point 0.20 2.83 0.77  radius 1.5

# THE LATCH UNDER THE THUMB. Part G puts a cylinder latch on a face button,
# which is `kind button`. The position is the body's outermost vertex in the
# slice immediately behind the cylinder face - x 0.92, y 0.37, z 0.01 - on the
# side the cylinder swings toward, which is where a Python's thumbpiece is.
# The frame is measurably thicker on that side: the slice runs x -0.55 to
# +0.92 about a bore on the centreline.
control mag_latch  at 0.92 0.37 0.01  finger thumb  kind button

# The firing chamber: SHELL03's rest position, the top chamber, the one under
# the barrel and under the hammer.
chamber at 0.01 0.33 0.85

# Where the brass leaves. Posed at frame 28 of `reload`, cylinder fully out:
# its rear face centre is at 1.97 0.29 -0.60. The chambers run along the bore
# axis, so cases come out along +Y, straight back - which is what tipping the
# muzzle up turns into a fall.
eject   at 1.97 0.29 -0.60  dir 0.00 1.00 0.00
